<IntegrationLayout title="Haliphron Google Read" description="Private, read-only Google account access for AI-assisted work: permissions, model-provider processing and how to disconnect.">
<p>Haliphron Google Read lets an authorized AI assistant find and read information from a connected Google account. Maxfield Allison operates this private connection for personal use and invited participants. There is no public signup.</p>
<p>The read service is operating for the operator's account. Its Google application configuration is being separated from the existing calendar-sync project. During that migration, Google may still identify the connection as Haliphron Calendar Sync. Contact the operator before revoking that shared application's access, since doing so can also stop calendar synchronization.</p>
<h2>What the connection reads</h2>
<p>The service supports Gmail messages and labels, Drive files, Calendar events, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Tasks and Contacts. A request can return message or document contents, file contents supported by the service, names and email addresses, event details, task text, and the identifiers needed to retrieve them. Files and calendars shared with the connected account may also be accessible.</p>
<p>The Google permission set is read-only: <code>gmail.readonly</code>, <code>drive.readonly</code>, <code>calendar.readonly</code>, <code>documents.readonly</code>, <code>spreadsheets.readonly</code>, <code>presentations.readonly</code>, <code>tasks.readonly</code> and <code>contacts.readonly</code>. These scope names use Google's <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/</code> prefix. Sign-in also requests <code>openid</code> and <code>userinfo.email</code> to identify the connected account.</p>
<p>Those permissions can read more than an individual search result. The service limits available operations, but the Google grant itself covers the corresponding readable account data. It cannot send mail, edit files, change events, delete tasks or modify contacts. Google Photos, account passwords and Google Cloud administration are not included.</p>
<h2>Where the information goes</h2>
<p>Google returns requested data to the operator's integration service. Results then enter the requesting assistant's conversation and can be processed by the AI provider used for that session, including OpenAI, Anthropic or Google. Connecting through a private server does not keep retrieved content away from the model provider.</p>
<p>Only connect an account when you agree to that processing. The selected service's account settings and terms govern its processing and conversation retention. Use this connection only with provider accounts and settings that limit retrieved Google data to the requested work and meet Google's Limited Use requirements. The operator does not use connected-account data to train general-purpose models.</p>
<p>Authorization credentials stay in protected storage used by the integration service; assistants receive tool results. Conversation histories, authorized summaries and operational records can retain retrieved information on the systems used for the work. Avoid requesting data that you are not permitted to share with the selected AI service. Shared access or family storage membership does not supply another person's consent.</p>
<h2>Limits and disconnecting</h2>
<p>AI summaries can be wrong or incomplete. Verify consequential information in the original Google service. A read-only Google connection can still disclose information through its results, so access is limited to authorized users and clients.</p>
<p>The <a href="/integrations/privacy">integration privacy policy</a> describes retention, operator access and deletion requests. The <a href="/integrations/terms">terms of use</a> apply. Removing access in <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" rel="noopener">Google Account connections</a> stops future authorized reads but does not erase existing conversations or copied results.</p>
<p>For access, support or deletion requests, contact <a href="mailto:maxfield.allison@gmail.com" data-umami-event="email-click">maxfield.allison@gmail.com</a>. Identify the application and account without sending passwords, tokens or private message contents.</p>
</IntegrationLayout>
